course: dictionary
lesson: 4558
title: Describing people
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Writers often choose one word to show what someone looks like. Heavyset is one of those words. It describes a person with a large, solid, broad body.
explain: Context gives you clues. In «The heavyset farmer lifted the sacks with ease», lifting heavy sacks easily tells you he is strong and solidly built, so heavyset must mean big and sturdy.
explain: Heavyset is a fairly polite way to describe someone's size. It is about how a body is built, not about what a person is like inside. Use it with care and kindness.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The heavyset boxer stepped into the ring» still makes sense with "big and solid" in place of heavyset, so the meaning fits.
fact: Heavyset is an adjective, a word that describes a noun.
fact: Heavy-set, with a hyphen, is another spelling of the same word.
fact: «Heavyset» means having a large, solid, broad body.
fact: «Heavyset» is often used in stories and in police descriptions of people.
fact: «Heavyset» is an American way to say fat or heavily built.
exercise: «The police described the thief as a heavyset man in a red coat.» What does heavyset describe? | A quiet voice | The colour of the coat | How fast the man ran | *A person's large, solid, broad body
exercise: «The heavyset farmer lifted the sacks with ease.» What do the words lifted the sacks with ease suggest? | He is very small and weak | He is a young child | *He is strong and solidly built | He is afraid of sacks
exercise: Which word means about the same as heavyset? | Tiny | Quick | Sleepy | *Big and sturdy
test: Heavyset means which of these? | Very fast | Very quiet | *Large, solid and broad | Thin and tall
test: In «The heavyset boxer stepped into the ring», which word could replace heavyset and keep the meaning? | Speedy | Hungry | *Solid and broad | Quiet
exam: Which is the best check when you meet a new word like heavyset? | *Swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense | Skip the whole text and never come back | Read the text backwards | Guess and never check
